lb = LabelBinarizer()
labels = lb.fit_transform(labels)
labels = to_categorical(labels)
What is One-Hot Encoding?

Computers cannot understand text labels directly.

Example:

mask
no_mask

We convert them into numbers.

Before One-Hot Encoding
mask     = 0
no_mask  = 1

Dataset:

0
1
0
1
After One-Hot Encoding
0 → [1, 0]
1 → [0, 1]

Result:

mask     → [1, 0]
no_mask  → [0, 1]
Why do we use it?

If we keep:

mask = 0
no_mask = 1

The model may think:

1 > 0

and assume one class is "larger" than the other.

But actually:

mask and no_mask are just categories

One-Hot Encoding removes this problem.

Example
Original Labels
labels = ['mask', 'no_mask', 'mask']
Label Encoding
[0, 1, 0]
One-Hot Encoding
[
 [1,0],
 [0,1],
 [1,0]
]
In Face Mask Detection
Class	Label	One-Hot
Mask	0	[1,0]
No Mask	1	[0,1]

When the model predicts:

[0.95, 0.05]

means

95% Mask
5% No Mask

Prediction:

Mask
Real-Time Example

Suppose camera captures a face.

Model output:

prediction = [0.12, 0.88]

Interpretation:

12% Mask
88% No Mask

Result:

No Mask Detected
